  {
    "id": "1793153663273",
    "name": "Lisa Vanderpump’s Shrimp Pasta",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/582bc704-3cc3-453d-b8e5-994249de352e.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;center,top&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "italian",
      "seafood",
      "european",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "20 min",
    "cookTime": "40 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "4 slices bacon, turkey bacon, or vegan bacon",
      "1 tbsp. unsalted butter",
      "1 tbsp. olive oil",
      "1 small red onion, diced",
      "2 garlic cloves, minced",
      "8 oz. (225 g) white button mushrooms, sliced",
      "1 tsp. garlic salt",
      "1/2 tsp. freshly ground black pepper",
      "1 1/2 cups (7 oz., 200 g) cherry tomatoes, halved crosswise",
      "12 fresh basil leaves, plus more for garnish",
      "1/2 cup (120 mL) dry white wine (such as Sauvignon Blanc)",
      "1 lb. (450 g) pasta of your choice, preferably long, thin noodles like spaghetti, as it really makes the most of the sauce",
      "1 lb. (450 g) peeled, deveined frozen shrimp, thawed and rinsed under cold water",
      "2 green onions, white and green parts, cut on a bias",
      "1/4 cup (30 g) grated Parmesan (optional)"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a large sauté pan, cook the bacon over medium heat until crispy, about 10 minutes. Remove from the pan to a paper towel-lined bowl. When it’s cool enough to handle, chop the bacon and set aside.",
      "In the same pan, warm the butter and olive oil over medium heat. Add the red onion and sauté until softened, about 5 minutes. Stir in the garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add the mushrooms; cook, stirring, until golden, 5 to 7 minutes. Season with the garlic salt and pepper. Stir in the cherry tomatoes and basil, tossing for 1 to 2 minutes, until they begin to soften. Pour in the white wine and continue to cook for 10 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the vegetables become pulpy.",
      "Meanwhile, bring a large pot of salted water to a boil over high heat. Add the pasta, give it a good stir to prevent it from sticking, and cook according to package directions until al dente. Do not overcook the pasta as it will be cooked when you bring it together in the sauce. Reserve 1/2 cup (120 mL) of the pasta water.",
      "Add the shrimp to the tomato-mushroom sauce. Cook and stir until the shrimp turn pink and opaque, flipping once, 3 to 4 minutes total. Reserve one ladleful of sauce to top the pasta.",
      "Toss the drained pasta into the remaining sauce along with the green onions, reserved bacon, and a splash of the reserved pasta water to bring the dish together. Add more of the reserved pasta water as needed; you may not need all of it. Taste and adjust the seasoning.",
      "Plate the pasta, spoon the reserved sauce over the top, and finish with Parmesan (if using) and fresh basil."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "Fresh off the release of her new cookbook, \"Home at Villa Rosa: Cooking and Living the Vanderpump Way,\" Lisa Vanderpump joined the Delish Test Kitchen to teach us how to make her shrimp pasta.",
    "videos": [
      {
        "url": "https://mos-streaming.hearst.io/d84124a6-dc60-4ddc-a47d-e0c35180de2e/video_16x9_1080p_h264_hd.mp4",
        "title": "Lisa Vanderpump's Shrimp Pasta",
        "thumbnailUrl": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/582bc704-3cc3-453d-b8e5-994249de352e.jpg?crop=0.889xw:1xh;0.056xw,0xh"
      }
    ]
  },
