    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "30 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 tbsp. extra-virgin olive oil",
      "1 yellow onion, thinly sliced",
      "1 red bell pepper, seeds and ribs removed, thinly sliced",
      "4 garlic cloves, finely chopped",
      "1 tsp. ground coriander",
      "1 tsp. sweet paprika",
      "3/4 tsp. ground cinnamon",
      "1/2 tsp. ground cumin",
      "1/4 tsp. cayenne pepper",
      "1 (14-oz.) can pumpkin puree",
      "2 cups canned crushed tomatoes",
      "1 1/2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "Freshly ground black pepper",
      "1/4 cup water",
      "6 Eggland’s Best large eggs",
      "4 oz. goat cheese",
      "Toasted pumpkin seeds, fresh cilantro leaves, and toasted bread, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a large, high-sided skillet over medium heat, heat oil. Add onion and pepper and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 7 minutes. Add garlic and cook, stirring, until fragrant, about 1 minute more.",
      "Push veggies to one side of skillet and add coriander, paprika, cinnamon, cumin, and cayenne to empty side. Cook, stirring, until fragrant, about 30 seconds, then stir spice mixture into veggies.",
      "Add pumpkin, tomatoes, salt, several grinds of pepper, and water and bring to a simmer. Let simmer, stirring occasionally, until slightly reduced, about 10 minutes. Taste and adjust seasonings as needed.",
      "Make 6 divots in sauce and crack an egg into each. Cover, reduce heat to medium-low, and cook until whites are set and yolks are still runny, 7 to 8 minutes. Remove from heat.",
      "Top with goat cheese, pumpkin seeds, and cilantro. Serve with bread alongside."
    ],
    "servings": "4 - 6 serving(s)",
    "description": "Classic shakshuka is such a simple dish to make and is good at all times of day, from brunch to dinner, but our pumpkin shakshuka has a little extra something that we can’t get enough of.",
