  {
    "id": "1793153663565",
    "name": "Pumpkin Horchata",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/51c75d54-9c1a-4f69-bcfc-0fd54365629d.jpg?crop=0.499916680553xw:1xh;center,top&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "drinks",
      "autumn",
      "breakfast"
    ],
    "drinkType": "non-alcoholic",
    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "480 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 cup long-grain white rice",
      "1/4 cup slivered almonds (optional)",
      "2 tsp. pumpkin pie spice",
      "6 cups filtered water, divided",
      "1 (15-oz.) can pumpkin puree",
      "1 (12-oz.) can evaporated milk",
      "2 cups whole milk or almond milk",
      "1/2 cup (or more) sweetened condensed milk",
      "2 tsp. pure vanilla extract",
      "1/2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "Ice and cinnamon sticks, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a blender, blend rice, almonds (if using), pumpkin spice, and 3 cups filtered water until rice is broken down but not completely pulverized, about 30 seconds. Transfer to a large container with a lid, cover, and refrigerate overnight.",
      "Return rice mixture to blender and blend until rice and almonds are finely pulverized, about 1 minute.",
      "Set a fine-mesh sieve over a large bowl with a spout or large glass measuring cup. Line sieve with a single layer of cheesecloth. (Do not double the cheesecloth, or it will be too thick to strain.)",
      "Pour rice mixture through cheesecloth-lined strainer, using a rubber spatula to press on pulp and release as much liquid as possible. Discard rice and almond pulp. Gather corners of cheesecloth and gently massage and squeeze to extract remaining liquid. (If you don’t mind a little sediment in your drink, you can skip the cheesecloth and pour mixture directly through sieve. If you prefer a smoother drink, the cheesecloth is worth the extra effort.)",
      "Rinse out blender, then return strained mixture to blender. Add pumpkin puree, evaporated milk, whole milk, condensed milk, vanilla, and salt. Blend until homogeneous, about 1 minute. Taste and add more condensed milk, if desired, blending after each addition.",
      "Transfer to a large pitcher and add remaining 3 cups filtered water. Refrigerate until ready to use.",
      "Serve over ice. Garnish with cinnamon sticks."
    ],
    "servings": "3 qt.",
    "description": "Classic horchata is always a go-to, but our pumpkin horchata really sets itself apart."
  },
  {
    "id": "1793153663652",
