  {
    "id": "1793153665834",
    "name": "Caesar Salad Deviled Eggs",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/3e048598-331d-4ce7-880d-6b8d7b6d6a5f.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;0.238xw,0xh&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "breakfast"
    ],
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "35 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "12 Eggland’s Best large eggs",
      "2 tsp. unsalted butter",
      "1/4 cup panko breadcrumbs",
      "Kosher salt",
      "Freshly ground black pepper",
      "1/3 cup mayonnaise",
      "2 oil-packed anchovy fillets, drained, finely chopped",
      "2 garlic cloves, grated",
      "2 tbsp. Dijon mustard",
      "2 tsp. fresh lemon juice",
      "2 tbsp. finely grated Parmesan",
      "2 romaine lettuce leaves, cut or torn into 1″ pieces"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Bring a large pot of water to a boil. (For 12 eggs, use about 4 qt. water.) Using a slotted spoon or tongs, gently lower eggs, one at a time, into water. Return to a boil, cover, and reduce heat to medium-low. Cook for 12 minutes.",
      "A few minutes before eggs are cooked, fill a large bowl with about 2 cups ice and about 3 cups water. Transfer eggs to ice bath. Let sit for about 30 seconds.",
      "Using the back of a spoon, tap each egg, making sure to tap all over shell. (Alternatively, you can tap and roll the eggs on a counter; keep in mind not to tap the eggs too hard!) Return cracked eggs to ice bath and let sit 5 minutes. Peel eggs under a thin stream of cool running water, or peel while still in ice water.",
      "Meanwhile, in a small saucepan over medium heat, melt butter. Add breadcrumbs and toss to coat. Cook, stirring occasionally, until breadcrumbs are deep golden brown, 5 to 6 minutes more; season with 1/4 tsp. salt and 1/4 tsp. pepper, then remove from heat.",
      "Halve eggs lengthwise and gently scoop out yolks into a medium bowl, arranging egg whites on a platter. Mash yolks with the back of a fork until broken down, then add anchovies, garlic, mayonnaise, mustard, and lemon juice; season with 1/4 tsp. salt and 1/4 tsp. pepper, then whisk until mostly smooth and pipeable.",
      "Transfer egg yolk mixture to a piping bag fitted with a round tip (or a resealable bag with a small corner snipped off). Pipe yolk mixture into egg whites. Top with toasted breadcrumbs, Parmesan, and romaine."
    ],
    "servings": "12 serving(s)",
    "description": "Our caesar salad deviled eggs are exactly the kind of app you need to make for your next girls’ night in or holiday party.",
    "videos": [
      {
        "url": "https://mos-streaming.hearst.io/6ccb3dca-451e-447f-9149-284c9668c71d/video_9x16_1080p_h264_hd.mp4",
