      "Arrange racks in upper and lower thirds of oven; preheat to 350°. In a large bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat butter, brown sugar, granulated sugar, and kosher salt until light and creamy, 1 to 2 minutes. Add egg, egg yolk, and vanilla and beat, scraping down sides of bowl as needed, until just combined. Add baking soda and beat until combined. Using a spatula, fold in flour and cocoa powder just until no streaks remain.",
