      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "215 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1/2 cup warm water (110°)",
      "2 (1/4-oz.) pkg. dry yeast",
      "1 tsp. sugar",
      "1 1/2 cups warm whole milk (110°)",
      "6 tbsp. (3/4 stick) unsalted butter, melted, cooled, plus more, softened, for greasing",
      "1 1/2 tbsp. honey",
      "2 extra-large egg yolks",
      "1 tbsp. kosher salt",
      "5 cups (600 g) (or more) all-purpose flour, divided, plus more for dusting",
      "1 extra-large egg white, lightly beaten"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Pour water into the large bowl of a stand mixer fitted with the dough hook. If bowl is cold, be sure water temperature doesn’t drop below 110°. Add yeast and sugar; stir and let dissolve for 5 minutes.",
      "Add milk, melted butter, and honey. Mix on medium speed until blended. Add egg yolks, salt, and 3 cups flour. Mix on low speed for about 5 minutes. With the mixer still on low speed, add 2 cups flour. Increase speed to medium and slowly add just enough flour so dough doesn’t stick to bowl. Add flour slowly; you can always add more, but you can’t take it out. Mix on medium speed for about 8 minutes, adding flour as necessary.",
      "Dump dough out onto a floured surface and knead by hand until smooth and elastic, about 1 minute. Grease a large bowl with softened butter, put dough in bowl, then turn it over so top is lightly buttered. Cover bowl with a damp towel and let rise until doubled in volume, about 1 hour.",
      "Grease 2 (9\" x 5\") loaf pans with butter. Divide dough in half, roll each half into a loaf shape, and place each in a prepared pan. Cover again with the damp towel and let rise until doubled in volume, about 1 hour.",
      "Meanwhile, arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 350°. When dough is ready, brush tops with egg white.",
      "Bake loaves until they sound hollow when tapped, 40 to 45 minutes. Turn them out of pans onto wire racks and let cool completely."
