    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "45 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 1/2 cups dried apricots",
      "1/4 tsp. saffron threads",
      "1 cup boiling water, divided",
      "2 garlic cloves, grated",
      "1/4 cup extra-virgin olive oil",
      "2 tsp. honey",
      "1 tsp. sweet paprika",
      "1/2 tsp. ground cinnamon",
      "1/2 tsp. ground cumin",
      "1/2 tsp. ground ginger",
      "1/2 tsp. ground turmeric",
      "2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "1 small preserved lemon",
      "2 lb. boneless, skinless chicken thighs",
      "2 small yellow onions, cut into 2\" chunks",
      "3 small carrots, peeled, thinly sliced on the bias",
      "1/2 cup mixed pitted olives",
      "1/4 cup coarsely chopped fresh cilantro"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Place apricots and saffron in separate heatproof bowls. Pour 1 Tbsp. boiling water over saffron, then pour remaining water over apricots. Let both steep until ready to use.",
      "In a large bowl, stir garlic, oil, honey, paprika, cinnamon, cumin, ginger, turmeric, and 2 tsp. salt.",
      "Cut lemon into quarters. Using a paring knife, separate flesh from peel. Coarsely chop flesh, removing seeds, and add to marinade. Thinly slice peel; set aside.",
      "Add saffron water to marinade, then add chicken, onion, and carrots and toss to coat. Let sit at least 30 minutes and up to overnight.",
      "Arrange a rack in upper third of oven; heat broiler. Spread chicken mixture on a foil-lined baking sheet. (It’s okay if some pieces of onion and carrot are under chicken.)",
      "Broil chicken, watching closely and rotating sheet halfway through, until browned, 8 to 9 minutes.",
      "Remove sheet from oven and flip chicken. Continue to broil until deeply browned and an instant-read thermometer inserted into thickest part registers 165°, 4 to 5 minutes more.",
      "Meanwhile, drain apricots and cut into quarters.",
      "Remove sheet from oven and add olives, apricots, and reserved lemon peel. Gently toss with onions, carrots, and sauce. Continue to broil, watching closely, until warmed through, 2 to 3 minutes.",
      "Transfer sheet to a wire rack. Top with cilantro."
    ],
