  {
    "id": "1793153669967",
    "name": "Pumpkin Pot Pie",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/b6f094cf-c9da-4972-a263-1dae93b2b9d3.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;0.239xw,0xh&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "autumn",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "25 min",
    "cookTime": "95 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "4 tbsp. unsalted butter",
      "1 medium yellow onion, finely chopped",
      "1 large carrot, peeled, finely chopped",
      "Kosher salt",
      "4 garlic cloves, finely chopped",
      "1 tbsp. fresh thyme",
      "1/4 cup red curry paste",
      "1 1/2 lb. fresh pumpkin, peeled, cut into 1/2″ cubes",
      "1/2 cup (60 g) all-purpose flour, plus more for dusting",
      "1 (13.5-oz.) can full-fat coconut milk, shaken",
      "3/4 cup low-sodium vegetable broth or water",
      "1 tbsp. finely chopped fresh basil",
      "1 lime, juiced",
      "2 ready-to-bake rolled pie crust doughs (about 14 oz.)",
      "1 large egg, beaten to blend",
      "Flaky sea salt"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 375°. In a large skillet over medium heat, melt butter. Cook onion, carrot, and a pinch of salt, stirring occasionally, until onion just begins to soften, about 5 minutes. Add garlic and thyme and cook, stirring, until fragrant, about 1 minute more.",
      "Stir in curry paste and cook, stirring, until paste starts to darken, 2 to 3 minutes. Add pumpkin and a pinch of salt and cook, stirring occasionally, until pumpkin starts to soften, 5 to 7 minutes.",
      "Sprinkle flour over vegetables and stir until no pockets of flour remain. Add milk and broth and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally, until mixture is slightly thickened, 2 to 3 minutes. Stir in basil and lime juice; season with salt, if needed. Let cool slightly, about 10 minutes.",
      "On a lightly floured surface, roll out a disc of dough to a 14″ round. Transfer to a deep 9″ pie dish, then add cooled filling.",
      "Carve a Jack-o’-lantern: Roll out second disc of dough to a 14″ round. Using a sharp paring knife, about one-third of the way down the round, carve 2 triangles for eyes. Carve a smaller triangle in the center for the nose. In the bottom third, carve a smile with two teeth at the bottom and one at the top (you can use stenciled parchment to help guide you). Arrange cutout dough on top of filling, then press edges of top and bottom rounds together.",
      "Using a sharp knife or kitchen shears, trim edges of dough, leaving a 1/4″ overhang. Fold excess dough underneath dough on top rim of pie dish. Using clean fingers, crimp to seal.",
      "In a small bowl, combine egg and 1 Tbsp. water. Brush top of dough with egg wash. Sprinkle with sea salt.",
      "Bake pot pie, checking at 45 minutes to make sure crust isn’t darkening too quickly and covering with foil if needed, until crust is golden brown, about 1 hour. Transfer to a wire rack and let cool at least 15 minutes before serving."
    ],
    "servings": "8 serving(s)",
    "description": "Whether you're hosting a Halloween party or simply looking for a cozy meatless dinner, our pumpkin pot pie is guaranteed to steal the show.",
