      "Shape into a disk and wrap in plastic wrap. Refrigerate until cold, about 1 hour.",
      "On a lightly floured surface, roll out dough until 1/8” thick. Cut out shapes with a football cookie cutter and transfer to 2 parchment-lined baking sheets. Freeze 10 minutes (so your shapes hold while baking!).",
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 350º. Bake cookies until edges are lightly golden, 8 to 10 minutes. Let cool completely.",
      "In a medium bowl, stir powdered sugar, corn syrup, milk, and vanilla. Measure out 1/4 cup white icing and set aside.",
      "To remaining icing, add food coloring and stir until desired color is reached. Transfer about one-third of brown icing to piping bag fitted with small round tip and outline cookies with icing.",
      "To remaining brown icing in bowl, add more confectioners' sugar if needed until icing is a good consistency to flood. Transfer icing to another piping bag fitted with small round tip. Fill in cookies with thinner icing. Sprinkle cookies with sanding sugar while still wet.",
      "Transfer reserved white icing to piping bag fitted with small round tip and pipe laces onto footballs. If cookies are still too wet to pipe laces on, freeze 15 minutes."
    ],
    "servings": "1 dz.",
    "description": "These football cookies are so easy to make with our perfect sugar cookie dough and icing. If you aren't a football fan yet, these cookies will do the trick.",
