    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/cinnamon-rolls-index-64777a26dea4f.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.269xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "breakfast",
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "30 min",
    "cookTime": "175 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "Cooking spray",
      "1 cup warm milk, heated to 110°",
      "2 1/4 tsp. or 1&nbsp;(0.25-oz.) packet&nbsp;instant yeast",
      "2 large eggs, room temperature",
      "4 1/2 cups (540 g.) all-purpose flour",
      "1/2 cup (100 g.)&nbsp;granulated sugar",
      "5 tbsp. unsalted butter, softened",
      "2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "1/4 tsp. baking soda",
      "3/4 cup (150 g.)&nbsp;packed light brown sugar",
      "2 tbsp. ground cinnamon",
      "1/2 tsp. ground nutmeg",
      "1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter, softened, divided, plus more for pan",
      "3/4 tsp. kosher salt, divided",
      "All-purpose flour, for surface",
      "6 oz. cream cheese, softened",
      "1 cup (120 g.)&nbsp;confectioners' sugar",
      "1 tsp. pure vanilla extract",
      "1/4 cup milk or&nbsp;heavy cream"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Lightly grease a large bowl with cooking spray. In another large bowl or in the large bowl of a stand mixer fitted with the dough hook, stir milk and yeast until yeast is mostly dissolved.&nbsp;",
      "Add eggs, flour, granulated sugar, butter, salt, and baking soda and beat on low speed until combined. Increase speed to medium-high and beat until dough is smooth and elastic and starts to pull away from sides of bowl, 10 to 15 minutes.",
      "Transfer dough to prepared bowl and turn so outside of dough is thoroughly greased. Cover with a kitchen towel and let rise until almost doubled in size, 1 to 2 hours.",
      "In a large bowl, using a handheld mixer, or in the large bowl of stand mixer fitted with the whisk attachment, cream brown sugar, cinnamon, nutmeg, 1/2 cup butter, and 1/2 teaspoon salt until light and fluffy, 3 to 4 minutes. Lightly grease a 13\"x 9\" baking pan with butter.",
      "On a lightly floured surface, dust dough with more flour. Using a rolling pin, roll out into a large square (about 18\"x 18\"). Spread to edges with filling, then roll dough into a log. Using a sharp knife, cut into 12 pieces, each about 1 1/2\" wide.",
      "Arrange rolls cut side up in prepared pan. Cover and let rise until almost doubled in size, 30 to 40 minutes.",
      "Preheat oven to 400°. Uncover rolls and bake until golden brown, 20 to 22 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, in large bowl using handheld mixer or in the large bowl of stand mixer with the paddle attachment, beat cream cheese, confectioners' sugar, vanilla, and remaining 1/2 cup butter and 1/4 teaspoon salt until light and fluffy. Gradually add milk and continue to beat to loosen icing.",
      "Immediately frost rolls. Serve warm."
    ],
    "servings": "12 serving(s)",
    "description": "This recipe perfects the soft and fluffy cinnamon roll—follow it to a T to go classic, or use it as a jumping off point to add your favorite flavors.",
    "videos": [
      {
        "url": "https://mos-streaming.hearst.io/a1ff6389-3c0d-4719-8cc8-68adacc050c3/video_rover_16x9_1080p_hd_1687960024_98355.mp4",
        "title": "Our Homemade Cinnamon Rolls Are The Ultimate Soft & Fluffy Brunch Treat",
        "thumbnailUrl": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/cinnamon-rolls-index-64777a26dea4f.jpg?crop=0.891xw:1.00xh;0.0554xw,0"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "1793153713573",
    "name": "Candied Sweet Potato Cinnamon Rolls",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/candied-sweet-potato-cinnamon-rolls-socialindex-web-080-del069925-68b72540c15b9.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.498xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "autumn",
      "breakfast",
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "40 min",
    "cookTime": "170 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 medium sweet potatoes (about 3/4 lb. total)",
      "1 cup whole milk",
      "1/2 cup (107 g.) packed dark brown sugar",
      "1 (1/4-oz.) packet rapid rise yeast",
      "4 cups (480 g.) all-purpose flour, plus more for dusting",
      "1/2 cup (1 stick) unsalted butter, softened",
      "1 tsp. kosher salt",
      "Vegetable oil, for greasing",
      "1 1/2 cups Marshmallow Fluff",
      "1 cup (57 g.) finely chopped&nbsp;pecans",
      "1/4 tsp. kosher salt",
      "2 tbsp. unsalted butter, softened",
      "All-purpose flour, for dusting",
      "1/2 cup mini marshmallows",
      "1/4 cup heavy cream",
      "1 cup (113 g.) confectioners' sugar",
      "1 tbsp. water",
      "1 tsp. pure vanilla extract"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Pierce potatoes all over with a fork. In a medium microwave-safe bowl, microwave potatoes until cooked through and fork-tender, 7 to 8 minutes. Let cool 10 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, in the large bowl of a stand mixer fitted with the dough hook, mix milk, brown sugar, and yeast until dissolved. Let sit until foamy, about 5 minutes.",
      "Cut potatoes in half lengthwise and scoop flesh (about 1 cup total) into a small bowl; discard skins. Whisk flesh until mostly smooth (a few bits and pieces are just fine). ",
      "Add flesh and flour to stand mixer bowl. Mix on medium speed until dough comes together. Increase speed to medium-high and continue to mix until smooth, about 10 minutes.",
      "Mix in butter and salt; you’ll notice the dough will start to separate, then come together again.",
      "On a lightly floured surface, turn out dough. Grease mixer bowl with oil. Return dough to bowl, cover, and let rise in a warm spot until doubled in size, 40 to 60 minutes.",
      "Grease a 13\" x 9\" baking dish with butter. Flour your hands and top of dough. Punch down dough to deflate. ",
      "Turn out dough on a lightly floured surface and roll out to an 18\" square. Using an offset spatula, spread filling over dough. Starting at one long edge, roll dough into a tight log and trim ends with a sharp knife. Cut log into 12 (1 1/2\"-thick) slices.",
      "Arrange rolls flat sides down in prepared dish. Cover and let rise until doubled in size, 40 to 60 minutes.",
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 400°. Uncover and bake rolls 15 minutes. Scatter marshmallows over top. Continue to bake until top is lightly golden, about 8 minutes more. Transfer to a wire rack and let cool 10 minutes. ",
      "Meanwhile, in a small saucepan over medium heat, cook brown sugar and cream, stirring, until sugar is just dissolved and mixture is warmed through, about 2 minutes.",
      "Transfer to a large bowl. Add confectioners’ sugar, water, and vanilla and whisk until smooth and glossy. Drizzle glaze over rolls.",
      "<strong>Make Ahead: </strong>Dough can be prepared through step 6 and refrigerated overnight. "
    ],
    "servings": "12",
    "description": "These candied sweet potato cinnamon rolls combine a sweet potato dough, pecans, marshmallows, and a brown sugar sticky glaze for the perfect fall treat.",
    "videos": [
      {
        "url": "https://mos-streaming.hearst.io/e2d16fcc-27ab-4167-81a9-d33b78e9e244/video_9x16_1080p_hd.mp4",
        "title": "Candied Sweet Potato Cinnamon Rolls",
        "thumbnailUrl": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/candied-sweet-potato-cinnamon-rolls-socialindex-web-080-del069925-68b72540c15b9.jpg?crop=0.2811792808649736xw:1xh;center,top"
      }
    ]
