    "instructions": [
      "Preheat&nbsp;oven to 450°.&nbsp;Put cauliflower in a large oven-safe skillet, rub all\r\nover with 2 tablespoons of melted butter, and season\r\nwith salt and pepper. Arrange garlic and herbs around\r\ncauliflower.&nbsp;",
      "Bake until cauliflower is tender and slightly charred,\r\nbrushing with remaining 2 tablespoons melted butter\r\nhalfway through, 1 hour to 1 hour 30 minutes. (Pierce\r\ncauliflower with a paring knife to check if it’s ready.)",
      "In a small saucepan over medium heat,&nbsp;melt butter. Add onion and cook, stirring until soft,\r\n\r\n5 minutes. Stir in mushrooms and herbs and season with\r\nsalt and pepper. Cook, stirring, until mushrooms are\r\n\r\nsoft and golden, about 4 minutes. Add 1 or 2 cloves of\r\nthe roasted garlic (skins removed), breaking up cloves\r\nwith a wooden spoon. Stir in flour and cook 1 minute,\r\nthen whisk in 2 cups of broth and bring mixture to a\r\nboil. Reduce heat to low and simmer until mixture has\r\nthickened to your desired consistency, 5 minutes. (Add\r\nmore broth if desired.)&nbsp;",
      "Serve cauliflower with gravy."
    ],
