    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a large bowl, whisk flour, granulated sugar, and salt. Add butter and rub into dry ingredients with your hands until butter is the size of walnut halves, making sure to toss and keep butter coated in flour. Add water and vinegar and toss to combine. Add more water 1 tablespoon at a time, if needed, until dough comes together when squeezed, is moist, and easily holds together, but isn’t wet and sticky.",
      "Form dough into a smooth disc and cover with plastic wrap. Refrigerate at least 2 hours or up to 3 days (or freeze up to 1 month).",
      "Let dough sit at room temperature 5 to 10 minutes. On a lightly floured surface, roll dough to a 12\" round. Unfurl into a 9\" pie plate and gently press dough into bottom and up sides of pan. Refrigerate until cold, about 10 minutes. ",
      "Trim edges, leaving a 1\" overhang. Tuck edges underneath so they’re flush with edge of pie plate, then crimp edges. Refrigerate until cold, about 15 minutes more. ",
