      "In a medium bowl, whisk&nbsp;flour, spices, baking soda, and salt&nbsp;until combined. With the mixer on low, gradually add dry ingredients to wet ingredients, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;fresh ginger, orange zest, and black pepper (if using),&nbsp;until dough just&nbsp;comes together. (Do not overmix!)",
      "Divide dough in half and create two discs. Wrap each in plastic wrap and chill until firm, about 2 to 3 hours. (Alternatively, divide dough in half and roll each piece of dough between two pieces of parchment to 1/4\" thick.&nbsp;Chill until firm.)",
      "<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-54679d99-d054-d2b8-68ed-028d5928f91a\"></span>Preheat oven to 350° and line two large baking sheets with parchment paper. Place one disc of dough on a lightly floured surface and roll until 1/4\" thick. (Alternatively, peel off both sheets of parchment from dough, then replace one sheet of parchment back underneath dough.) Cut out gingerbread men with a 3\" wide cutter&nbsp;and transfer to baking sheets.",
      "<span id=\"docs-internal-guid-54679d99-d055-6ba2-53c9-4766101c7c97\"></span>Bake until slightly puffed and set, 9 to 10 minutes, depending on the size of your cookie cutters. Let cool on baking sheets for 5 minutes before transferring to a cooling rack to cool completely.&nbsp;",
      "&nbsp;Repeat with remaining disc of dough. Decorate with icing and sprinkles as desired."
