      "Place cauliflower in a large cast-iron skillet. (If stem is too long for cauliflower to sit flush with pan, cut off excess stem.) Rub cauliflower with a thin layer of oil; season with salt, making sure to distribute over entire head. Brush cauliflower with half of garlicky oil. Loosely cover with foil.",
