      "Reduce heat to medium. In same pot, cook potatoes cut side down, undisturbed, until slightly softened, about 5 minutes. Add carrots and shallots; season with salt and black pepper. Stir to release potatoes. Return brisket and any accumulated juices to pot. Pour cider and broth over and add thyme and bay leaves. Add cayenne; season with salt and black pepper and stir to combine. Cover and bring to a boil.&nbsp;",
