      "Using a 1/4-c. measuring cup, scoop latke mixture and shape into patties about 3 1/2\" wide. Working 3 or 4 at a time, slide latkes into hot oil with a metal fish spatula.",
      "Fry latkes, undisturbed, until golden brown on the bottom 3 to 4 minutes. Carefully flip and continue to fry until golden brown on the other side, 2 to 3 minutes more. Transfer to prepared rack; immediately season with salt. Repeat with remaining patties."
    ],
    "servings": "10 serving(s)",
    "description": "Crispy-crunchy on the outside, soft and fluffy inside, these latkes are the best parts of a hash brown and a potato pancake all rolled into one. ",
