      "To bowl with celery mixture, add egg, mayonnaise, mustard, parsley, Cajun seasoning, Worcestershire, lemon pepper seasoning, and black pepper and whisk to combine. Using a spatula, gently fold in crabmeat and crushed crackers without breaking up meat too much. Using a 1/4-cup measuring cup, portion crabmeat mixture into 10 patties.",
      "Wipe skillet clean. In same skillet over medium heat, heat 2 Tbsp. oil until shimmering. Add 5 patties and cook, turning halfway through, until both sides are deep golden brown, 3 to 4 minutes. Transfer to a plate. Repeat with remaining 2 Tbsp. oil and 5 patties. ",
