    "cookTime": "90 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "Cooking spray",
      "1 oz. freeze-dried strawberries",
      "1/3 cup strawberry jam (not jelly)",
      "Kosher salt",
      "1 cup (200 g) granulated sugar",
      "1/3 cup packed light brown sugar",
      "1 vanilla bean, split lengthwise, seeds scraped, or 2 tsp. vanilla bean paste (optional)",
      "3/4 cup (1 1/2 sticks) unsalted butter, melted, room temperature",
      "2 large eggs, room temperature",
      "3/4 cup sour cream, room temperature",
      "1 tsp. pure vanilla extract",
      "2 tbsp. plus 2 tsp. fresh lemon juice, divided",
      "1 1/2 cups (180 g) all-purpose flour",
      "1 1/2 tsp. baking powder",
      "3/4 cup (85 g) confectioners’ sugar, sifted"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 350°. Coat an 8 1/2\" x 4 1/2\" loaf pan with cooking spray. Line with a strip of parchment, leaving an overhang on 2 short opposite sides.",
      "In a blender, food processor, or spice mill, blend strawberries to a fine powder. Measure out 1 Tbsp. strawberry powder; reserve for glaze. In a small bowl, mix jam, 2 heaping Tbsp. strawberry powder, and a pinch of salt until combined.",
      "In a large bowl, whisk granulated sugar and brown sugar until combined. Rub vanilla seeds (if using) into sugars until fragrant. Add butter and 1 tsp. salt and whisk until smooth. Add eggs, one at a time, whisking to blend after each addition. Add sour cream, vanilla extract, and 2 tsp. lemon juice and whisk to combine. Add flour and baking powder and whisk just until smooth, being sure to not overmix.",
      "Pour one-quarter of batter into prepared pan, evenly spreading. Gently spoon small amounts of jam mixture over, making sure to not let it touch sides of pan (it will caramelize during the long bake). Repeat 3 times with remaining batter and 2 times with remaining jam mixture, alternating and ending with batter. Using a chopstick or small butter knife, gently swirl batter and jam together, then smooth top.",
      "Bake cake 30 minutes. Reduce oven temperature to 325° and continue to bake until a tester inserted into the center comes out clean with a few moist crumbs attached, 30 to 40 minutes.",
      "Let cool 15 minutes, then invert cake onto a wire rack. Let cool completely.",
      "Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, whisk confectioners’ sugar, reserved strawberry powder, a pinch of salt, and remaining 2 Tbsp. lemon juice until smooth. Add a small splash of water or milk if glaze is too thick.",
      "Pour glaze over cake, then spread to coat top. Let sit at room temperature until glaze is set, 15 to 20 minutes."
    ],
