    "name": "Baklava Cheesecake",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/del089924-baklavacheesecake-web-252-rv-index-66e3b2055be2e.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.353xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "650 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 cup roasted, salted, shelled pistachios, plus more for topping",
      "1 cup walnut halves",
      "1 tsp. ground cinnamon",
      "1 cup honey, divided&nbsp;",
      "3/4 tsp. kosher salt, divided&nbsp;",
      "3/4 cup (1 1/2 sticks) unsalted butter, melted&nbsp;",
      "14 (18\" x 14\") sheets phyllo dough, thawed&nbsp;",
      "3 (8-oz.) pkg. cream cheese, room temperature",
      "1/4 cup sour cream",
      "1/4 cup pistachio cream&nbsp;",
      "3 large eggs&nbsp;",
      "2 tbsp. all-purpose flour&nbsp;",
      "1 navel orange, zested and juiced"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 350°. In a food processor, pulse pistachios, walnuts, cinnamon, 1/4 c. honey, and 1/2 tsp. salt until finely chopped, about 30 seconds.",
      "Brush bottom and sides of 9\" springform pan with some butter until coated. Place a sheet of phyllo in pan, lining bottom and sides of pan, letting excess hang over the sides. Brush surface of phyllo with butter, excluding dough hanging over the sides. Repeat with 4 more sheets, rotating the orientation of each sheet for an even overhang, for a total of 5 layers.",
      "Top phyllo with half of pistachio mixture, pressing into an even layer. Top with a sheet of phyllo; brush with butter. Repeat with another 4 sheets of phyllo to create 5 more layers. Refrigerate remaining phyllo.",
      "Trim overhang so that it no longer curls over rim of pan. Place scraps in pan and brush with butter. Reserve remaining butter.<br>",
      "Bake crust until golden brown, about 30 minutes. Let cool slightly. Wrap bottom of pan in foil and place in a large roasting pan.",
      "In clean food processor, pulse cream cheese, pistachio cream, sour cream, and 1/2 c. honey until smooth. Add eggs, one at a time, pulsing after each addition. Add flour, orange zest, and 1/4 tsp. salt and pulse until smooth.",
      " In a medium heatproof bowl, microwave orange juice and remaining 1/4 c. honey until syrup is slightly thickened, about 2 minutes. Combine half of orange syrup with reserved butter; reserve remaining orange-honey syrup for serving.",
      "Reduce oven temperature to 325°. Pour cheesecake batter over baklava crust. Top with all but 2 Tbsp. of remaining pistachio mixture.",
      "With long edge of phyllo facing you cut in half crosswise. Brush with butter-syrup mixture. Gently scrunch the edges of sheets toward the center to make a rope. Place one scrunched phyllo rope around outer edge of crust on top of pistachio layer. Place second phyllo rope along the edge on the other side. Repeat with remaining 2 sheets of phyllo, working your way to the center. Sprinkle with reserved 2 Tbsp. pistachio mixture.",
      "Transfer pan to oven and pour enough boiling water into roasting pan to come halfway up sides of springform pan. Bake cheesecake until slightly jiggly and phyllo is golden, about 1 hour, 45 minutes. Turn off oven, prop open door, and let cool in oven, about 1 hour. Refrigerate until cold, at least 8 hours or up to 12.",
      "Release cake from pan and transfer to a platter. Sprinkle with chopped pistachios. Serve with remaining orange-honey syrup alongside."
    ],
    "servings": "16 serving(s)",
    "description": "Pistachio orange cheesecake with a walnut and pistachio baklava crust and a honey syrup drizzle makes for the ultimate impressive dessert. ",
