    "instructions": [
      "Arrange racks in upper and lower thirds of oven; preheat to 350°. Line 3 (8\") round pans with parchment.",
      "In a large bowl, whisk cake mix, egg whites, wine, oil, orange zest, and salt. Stir in red and purple food coloring until desired color is reached. Divide batter among prepared pans.",
      "Bake cakes until a tester inserted into the centers comes out clean, 15 to 17 minutes.",
      "Transfer pans to wire racks and let cool.",
      "In a large bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed (or in the large bowl of a stand mixer fitted with the paddle attachment), beat butter until fluffy. Add confectioners’ sugar and beat until combined, then gradually beat in brandy, 1 Tbsp. at a time. Add salt and beat until smooth.",
      "Spoon a dab of frosting onto a platter (to keep cake in place). Place first cake on platter and top with frosting. Smooth into an even layer, then scatter with half of blueberries, half of raspberries, and half of strawberries. Repeat process with second cake, topping with frosting and remaining fruit, then top with final cake.",
