  {
    "id": "1793153781735",
    "name": "Banana Cream Pie",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/banana-cream-pie-index-682ba64017ae9.jpeg?crop=0.566xw:1.00xh;0.144xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "20 min",
    "cookTime": "100 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 batch&nbsp;basic pie dough",
      "All-purpose flour, for surface",
      "4 large egg yolks",
      "1 tsp. pure vanilla extract",
      "2 cups (475 ml.) whole milk",
      "1/2 cup (100 g.) granulated sugar",
      "3 tbsp. cornstarch",
      "1/4 tsp. kosher salt",
      "3 tbsp. unsalted butter, cut into 1/2\" pieces",
      "5 (or more)&nbsp;medium bananas (about 2 lb.; 905 g. total), divided",
      "1 cup (235 ml.) heavy whipping cream",
      "Toasted coconut chips, optional"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "On a lightly floured surface, roll pie dough into a 12” circle (between ¼” and ⅛” thick). Drape over a 9” pie dish and gently press to fit (don’t stretch), then trim crust to ½” beyond rim of dish with a paring knife or kitchen shears. Fold under overhang so it extends slightly beyond edge of pie dish. Crimp edge as desired. Prick bottom of crust all over with a fork. Refrigerate until dough is firm, about 30 minutes.&nbsp;",
      "In a medium bowl, use a whisk to beat egg yolks and vanilla until well combined; set aside.",
      "In a large bowl, prepare an ice bath. In a large saucepan, whisk milk, sugar, cornstarch, and salt together until smooth. Bring to a gentle simmer over medium heat, stirring often. Cook, stirring constantly, until thickened, 2 to 3 minutes. Remove from heat.&nbsp;",
      "Gradually whisk in 1/2 cup milk mixture into eggs until well combined. Gradually whisk egg-milk mixture into remaining milk mixture in saucepan. Bring to a simmer over medium heat, stirring frequently. Cook, stirring constantly, until thickened, 2 to 4 minutes. Remove from heat and stir in butter until completely melted. Transfer to a large bowl or measuring cup and cover with plastic wrap, pressing onto surface of pastry cream to prevent a skin from forming. Place in ice bath until slightly cooled, 15 minutes. Transfer to refrigerator to cool completely, 30 to 40 minutes, or up to 1 day.&nbsp;",
      "Meanwhile, bake crust: preheat oven to 375° with rack in center of oven. Line chilled crust with parchment paper, leaving a 1” overhang. Fill with pie weights, dried beans, or rice. Bake until golden around edges, 20 to 25 minutes. Lift parchment to remove pie weights. Return crust to oven, and continue baking until deeply golden, 12 to 15 minutes more. Place pie shell on a wire rack to cool completely.&nbsp;",
      "Slice 2 to 3 bananas on bias into ¼”-thick slices. Arrange slices on bottom of cooled pie crust, overlapping slightly, until bottom of crust is completely covered.&nbsp;",
      "Gently spread cooled pastry cream in an even layer on top of bananas. Press plastic wrap onto surface of pastry cream (this prevents a skin from forming on surface). Refrigerate for at least 2 hours or up to 1 day.&nbsp;",
      "Before serving, whip cream to soft peaks. Dollop whipped cream on top of pie leaving a 1” border. Slice remaining bananas on bias into ¼”-thick slices and arrange on top of whipped cream as desired. Top with coconut chips, if using. Slice into wedges."
    ],
    "servings": "8 serving(s)",
    "description": "With a thick and creamy pastry cream, bananas, whipped cream, toasted coconut chips, and a flaky pie crust, this easy banana cream pie is bakery-worthy. ",
    "videos": [
      {
