      "Meanwhile, spread almonds in a single layer on another unlined baking sheet. Roast on top rack until golden in the center, 8 to 10 minutes. Let cool 5 minutes.",
      "Transfer almonds to food processor and pulse until finely chopped. Transfer to bowl with beans.",
      "In a large skillet over medium heat, heat 1 tablespoon oil. Add onion, garlic, and 1/2 teaspoon salt. Cook, stirring occasionally, until onion is translucent and sweet to the taste, 6 to 8 minutes. Transfer to bowl with beans.",
      "In food processor, pulse mushrooms until finely chopped but not pastey. In same skillet over medium heat, heat remaining 1 tablespoon oil. Add mushrooms and cook, stirring often, until excess moisture has evaporated and mushrooms are beginning to stick to bottom of skillet, 4 to 6 minutes. Season with remaining 1/2 teaspoon salt and transfer to bowl with beans.",
      "Add feta, panko, and paprika to bowl. Using a rubber spatula, lightly toss to combine. Add egg and mayonnaise and continue to stir, folding and compacting mixture until it holds together when squeezed.",
      "Line reserved baking sheet with parchment. Using clean hands, form bean mixture into 8 patties (about 4 1/4 oz. each; 1/3\" thick and 3 1/2\" wide). Arrange on prepared sheet and refrigerate until cold, at least 2 hours or up to 3 days in an airtight container.",
      "In a small bowl, stir chopped chile and adobe sauce, mayonnaise, and salt. Cover and refrigerate until ready to use.",
      "<strong>For grilling:</strong> Prepare a grill for medium-low heat; preheat 5 minutes. Clean and oil grates. Grill patties until browned on the bottom, about 4 minutes, then flip and continue to grill until warmed through and charred on second side (an instant-read thermometer should register 165°), about 4 minutes more.",
      "<strong>For stovetop:</strong> In a large, heavy skillet over medium-low heat, heat 3 tablespoons oil. Cook 2 patties, undisturbed, until browned on the bottom, about 4 minutes. Turn and cook until browned on second side and warmed through (an instant-read thermometer should register 165°), about 4 minutes more. Repeat with remaining patties and oil.",
      "Arrange lettuce leaves on bottom buns. Top each with a burger, tomato, and onion."
    ],
    "servings": "8 serving(s)",
    "description": "Made with black beans and mushrooms and topped with a chipotle mayo, these veggie burgers will make even meat lovers decide to go meatless for a meal.",
    "videos": [
