      "Meanwhile, bring a medium pot of water to a boil; season with 1 Tbsp. salt. Set a medium bowl of ice water next to pot. Cook shrimp, stirring frequently, until pink and just cooked through, about 2 minutes. Using a spider or slotted spoon, transfer shrimp to ice water and let cool 2 minutes. Pat dry.",
      "Add bell pepper, tomatoes, cilantro, Old Bay, shrimp, and pasta to bowl with onion mixture. Drizzle with oil, then toss to combine; season with salt, if needed."
