  {
    "id": "1793153796688",
    "name": "Caesar Grilled Asparagus",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/eb7cc234-629b-4a53-beb9-9de02c198ce4.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.250xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "italian",
      "side-dish",
      "european"
    ],
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "20 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 1/2 oz. Parmesan, finely grated (about 3/4 cup)",
      "1/2 cup mayonnaise",
      "2 tbsp. fresh lemon juice",
      "1 1/2 tsp. Worcestershire sauce",
      "1 tsp. anchovy paste",
      "1 tsp. Dijon mustard",
      "1/2 tsp. garlic powder",
      "1/2 tsp. freshly ground black pepper",
      "1/8 tsp. kosher salt",
      "2 lb. asparagus, trimmed",
      "1/4 tsp. freshly ground black pepper",
      "4 tbsp. extra-virgin olive oil, divided",
      "1/2 tsp. kosher salt, divided",
      "2 (or more) slices sourdough or country-style bread",
      "1/2 tsp. Italian seasoning",
      "1/4 tsp. garlic powder",
      "Finely grated Parmesan, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a medium bowl, whisk Parmesan, mayonnaise, lemon juice, Worcestershire, anchovy paste, mustard, garlic powder, pepper, and salt until combined.",
      "Cover bowl and refrigerate until ready to use.",
      "Prepare a grill for high heat; preheat 5 minutes (or heat a grill pan over high heat). On a large baking sheet, toss asparagus, pepper, 2 Tbsp. oil, and 1/4 tsp. salt.",
      "Grill asparagus, arranging perpendicular to grates so they don’t fall through and turning occasionally, until charred and tender, 2 to 3 minutes (3 to 4 minutes if using grill pan). Transfer asparagus to a platter.",
      "Reduce heat to medium-low. In a small bowl, combine Italian seasoning, garlic powder, and remaining 2 Tbsp. oil and 1/4 tsp. salt. Brush seasoned oil onto both sides of bread.",
      "Grill bread, turning occasionally, until toasted, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Transfer to a plate and let cool slightly.",
      "Cut bread into cubes or tear into bite-sized pieces.",
      "Top asparagus with desired amount of dressing, croutons, and Parmesan. Serve with remaining dressing alongside."
    ],
    "servings": "4 - 6 serving(s)",
    "description": "While we love a basic  Caesar salad, this recipe focuses on charred and tender asparagus, adding herb-garlic grilled croutons to bring a level of flavor that romaine and oven-baked croutons just can’t match. ",
