  {
    "id": "1793153815319",
    "name": "Red, White  Blue Cheesecake Lasagna",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/7eac061d-dae9-4ce7-9c74-e787f9d4916a.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;0.451xw,0xh&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "240 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 cups cold water, divided",
      "2/3 cup cornstarch, divided",
      "24 oz. fresh blueberries, plus more for serving (optional)",
      "1 1/2 cups (300 g) granulated sugar, divided",
      "1/4 tsp. kosher salt, divided",
      "1 tbsp. fresh lemon juice",
      "24 oz. fresh strawberries, hulled, finely chopped",
      "10 tbsp. unsalted butter, melted",
      "2 tbsp. granulated sugar",
      "1/2 tsp. kosher salt, divided",
      "2 3/4 cups (10 oz.) finely crushed graham cracker crumbs (from about 18 crackers)",
      "12 oz. cream cheese, softened",
      "3/4 cup (85 g) plus 3 Tbsp. confectioners’ sugar",
      "2 1/2 cups heavy cream, divided",
      "Whole fresh blueberries and finely chopped fresh strawberries, for serving (optional)"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Blueberry Compote: In a small bowl, whisk 1/3 cup water and 1/3 cup cornstarch.",
      "In a medium pot over medium-high heat, bring blueberries, 2/3 cup water, 3/4 cup (150 g) granulated sugar, and 1/8 tsp. salt to a boil. Cook, crushing berries with a potato masher or back of a spoon, until berries are softened and mostly broken down, 2 to 3 minutes.",
      "Whisk cornstarch slurry again to reincorporate, then whisk into blueberry compote; reserve small bowl. Reduce heat to medium and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring often, until mixture reduces to a thick jam, 3 to 4 minutes.",
      "Stir in lemon juice, then transfer to a medium heatproof bowl and let cool at room temperature, about 45 minutes.",
      "Strawberry Compote: In reserved small bowl, whisk 1/3 cup water and remaining 1/3 cup cornstarch until combined.",
      "In another medium pot over medium-high heat, bring strawberries and remaining 2/3 cup water, 3/4 cup (150 g) granulated sugar, and 1/8 tsp. salt to a boil. Cook, crushing berries with potato masher or back of spoon, until strawberries are softened and mostly broken down, 2 to 3 minutes.",
      "Whisk cornstarch slurry again to reincorporate, then whisk into strawberry compote. Bring to a simmer and cook, stirring often, until mixture reduces to a thick jam, 4 to 5 minutes. Transfer to another medium heatproof bowl and let cool at room temperature, about 45 minutes.",
      "When compotes are almost cooled, in a large bowl, stir butter, granulated sugar, and 1/4 tsp. salt. Pour in graham crackers and stir to combine. Evenly press into bottom of a 13\" x 9\" (preferably glass) baking dish. Refrigerate until firm, at least 15 minutes and up to 1 hour.",
      "In another large bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat cream cheese, 3/4 cup (85 g) confectioners’ sugar, and remaining 1/4 tsp. salt until smooth and creamy, 1 to 2 minutes. Add 1 1/4 cups cream and beat on low speed until combined, about 30 seconds. Increase speed to medium-high and continue to beat until light and fluffy, 30 to 60 seconds more.",
      "Spread cooled blueberry compote onto crust, smoothing top with a mini offset spatula or the back of a spoon. Drop small dollops of cream cheese mixture to cover top of compote (I recommend about 20 small dollops); carefully spread to cover. Carefully spread cooled strawberry compote on top.",
      "Refrigerate until cold and set, at least 3 hours and up to overnight.",
      "When ready to serve, in a medium bowl, using handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat remaining 1 1/4 cups cream and 3 Tbsp. confectioners’ sugar until stiff peaks form.",
      "Spread whipped cream over strawberry filling. Decorate with more strawberries and blueberries, as desired."
    ],
    "servings": "12 serving(s)",
