    "id": "1793153834045",
    "name": "3-Ingredient Chocolate Marshmallow Mousse",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/3-ingredient-chocolate-marshmallow-mousse-socialindex-web-050-lp-del029926-6994dd356673b.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.234xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "5 min",
    "cookTime": "40 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "12 oz. 60% cacao chocolate chips or coarsely chopped chocolate",
      "4 oz. mini marshmallows",
      "1/4 tsp. kosher salt",
      "1/2 cup warm water",
      "2 1/2 cups heavy cream, divided",
      "Fresh strawberries, for topping (optional)"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a medium microwave-safe bowl, microwave chocolate, marshmallows, and salt in 30-second intervals, stirring between each, until melted and smooth, about 2 minutes total. Stir in water, 1/4 cup at a time (this makes it easier to incorporate into the stiffer chocolate mixture). Let cool to room temperature.",
      "Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat 2 cups cream until medium peaks form, 5 to 6 minutes.",
      "Stir marshmallow mixture to ensure it’s smooth and completely cooled, then add one-third of whipped cream. Using a flexible rubber spatula, fold cream into chocolate mixture by scooping around the sides of the bowl, then down through the middle until only a few white streaks remain. Add another third of remaining whipped cream, folding in as before, then repeat with the final third, folding until no streaks remain.",
      "Carefully spoon mousse into serving glasses. Refrigerate, uncovered, until cold and set, about 30 minutes.",
      "When ready to serve, in a medium bowl, using handheld mixer on medium speed, whip remaining 1/2 cup cream until medium peaks form, 4 to 5 minutes.",
      "Top mousse with whipped cream and garnish with strawberries (if using)."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "With this simple cheat recipe, it only takes three ingredients and two bowls to make chocolate mousse.",
