      "1 cup shredded cheddar"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a medium pot over medium heat, heat 1 Tbsp. oil. Add onion and cook, stirring occasionally, until softened, about 7 minutes. Add garlic and cook, stirring frequently, until fragrant, about 1 minute more. Add tomato paste and stir to coat onion and garlic. Add beef and cook, breaking up meat with a wooden spoon, until no longer pink, about 7 minutes. Drain excess fat, if needed.",
      "Add chili powder and paprika; season with salt and pepper. Add beans and tomato sauce. Bring to a boil over high heat, then reduce heat to medium and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally, until slightly reduced and flavors have melded, about 15 minutes.",
      "Spoon some beef mixture into center of each tortilla, leaving room to fold in edges. Top with Fritos, then cheddar. Fold edges of tortillas toward the center, creating 5 to 6 pleats. Invert Crunchwraps so pleats are on the bottom and stay together.",
      "In medium skillet over medium heat, heat remaining 1 Tbsp. oil. Add a Crunchwrap seam side down and cook, turning halfway through, until tortilla is golden, 3 to 5 minutes per side. Repeat with remaining Crunchwraps."
