    "id": "1793153839277",
    "name": "One-Pan Creamy Harissa Chickpeas",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/one-pan-creamy-harissa-chickpeas-socialindex-web-045-lp-del029926-6994d8d4be96b.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.250xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "vegan",
      "dinner",
      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "20 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "2 tbsp. extra-virgin olive oil",
      "1/2 yellow onion, finely chopped",
      "1 tsp. (or more) kosher salt, divided",
      "3 garlic cloves, finely chopped",
      "1/4 to 1/3 cup harissa sauce (such as Mina Spicy), according to heat preference",
      "1/4 cup tomato paste",
      "2 (14.5-oz.) cans chickpeas, drained, rinsed",
      "1/4 tsp. baking soda",
      "1 (14.5-oz.) can unsweetened full-fat coconut milk, well shaken",
      "4 oz. baby spinach (about 4 cups)",
      "Pita, for serving (optional)"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a large skillet over medium heat, heat oil. Add onion; season with 1/2 tsp. salt. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and translucent, about 7 minutes. Add garlic and cook, stirring, until fragrant, about 1 minute more.",
      "Add harissa and tomato paste and cook, stirring constantly, until darkened and starting to stick to bottom of skillet pan, 3 to 4 minutes. Add chickpeas and baking soda; season with 1/2 tsp. salt and toss until combined.",
      "Add coconut milk and bring to a simmer. Cook, stirring occasionally and adjusting heat as needed to maintain a low simmer, until slightly reduced, 3 to 4 minutes. Stir in spinach until wilted, about 1 minute more; season with salt, if needed.",
      "Serve warm with pita, if desired."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "Harissa, tomato paste, and coconut milk join forces with chickpeas to create a saucy weeknight one-pan dinner that’s as quick to make as it is wildly craveable.",
