      "In a large (12\") cast-iron skillet over medium heat, heat oil and 4 Tbsp. butter until butter has melted and begins to sizzle.",
      "Dredge chicken in flour mixture and shake off any excess. Place chicken, skin side down, in skillet and cook over medium heat without moving for 12 minutes. With chicken still skin side down, place skillet in oven and roast for 10 minutes.",
      "Return skillet to the stovetop over medium heat (careful; the handle will be hot!). Turn chicken skin side up, add remaining 5 Tbsp. butter, and continue to cook until butter is a nutty brown color and chicken is just cooked through (an instant-read thermometer will register 130° to 140°), 3 to 5 minutes. Remove from heat. Sprinkle with parsley.",
