    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/6ebd07c3-8b3e-4657-af55-50407e193e25.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;center,top&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "asian",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "20 min",
    "cookTime": "25 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "Cooking spray",
      "1 large egg",
      "1/3 cup milk",
      "1/3 cup panko breadcrumbs",
      "2 lb. ground chicken",
      "4 scallions, thinly sliced",
      "1 (1\") piece ginger, peeled, grated",
      "1 garlic clove, grated",
      "1 1/2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "1/2 tsp. freshly ground black pepper",
      "1 (2\") piece ginger, peeled, grated",
      "2 garlic cloves, grated",
      "1/2 cup honey",
      "6 tbsp. low-sodium soy sauce",
      "2 tbsp. cornstarch",
      "2 tbsp. unseasoned rice vinegar",
      "4 tsp. toasted sesame oil",
      "Toasted sesame seeds and thinly sliced scallions, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 425°. Grease a standard 12-cup muffin tin with cooking spray.",
      "In a large bowl, stir egg, milk, and panko until combined. Let sit until panko is softened, about 5 minutes.",
      "Add chicken, scallions, ginger, garlic, salt, and pepper. Using a rubber spatula or clean hands, mix until combined. Spoon about 1/3 cup chicken mixture into each well of prepared muffin tin; press down to flatten.",
      "Bake meatballs for 15 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, in a small saucepan, whisk ginger, garlic, honey, soy sauce, cornstarch, vinegar, oil, and 1/2 cup water. Cook over medium heat, stirring frequently, until thickened, about 3 minutes.",
      "Remove meatballs from oven. Brush tops of each with about 2 Tbsp. sauce.",
      "Continue to bake until an instant-read thermometer inserted into a meatball registers 165°, 10 to 15 minutes more.",
      "Sprinkle with sesame seeds and scallions."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "Our teriyaki meatloaf bites transform humble ground chicken into an easy weeknight meal featuring our favorite Asian-inspired flavors."
  },
  {
    "id": "1793153849325",
    "name": "Peanut Chicken Meatballs",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/20007226-de17-4caa-8259-751b57d2f0a1.jpg?crop=0.5xw:1xh;0.238xw,0xh&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "asian",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "20 min",
    "cookTime": "30 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 large egg",
      "3/4 cup panko breadcrumbs",
      "6 garlic cloves, finely chopped, divided",
      "4 tbsp. minced or grated peeled ginger, divided",
      "2 tbsp. finely chopped fresh basil, plus whole leaves for serving",
      "1 (14.5-oz) can unsweetened coconut milk, divided",
      "5 tbsp. low-sodium soy sauce, divided",
      "1/4 tsp. (or more) kosher salt",
      "1 lb. ground chicken",
      "3 tbsp. neutral oil, divided",
      "3 tbsp. Thai red curry paste",
      "1/4 cup creamy sweetened peanut butter (such as Skippy’s)",
      "1 red bell pepper, seeds and ribs removed, thinly sliced",
      "2 tbsp. (or more) fresh lime juice",
      "1/4 cup unsalted roasted peanuts",
      "Fresh cilantro leaves and tender stems, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a large bowl, whisk egg until homogeneous. Add panko, 2 garlic cloves, 2 Tbsp. ginger, 2 Tbsp. chopped basil, 2 Tbsp. coconut milk, and 1 Tbsp. soy sauce; season with 1/4 tsp. salt and stir until combined. Add chicken and fold until tacky to the touch.",
      "Using gloved or wet hands, divide chicken mixture into 14 (1.5-oz.) portions and roll into balls. Arrange on a parchment-lined baking sheet.",
      "In a large skillet over medium heat, heat 2 Tbsp. oil. Arrange meatballs in a single layer and cook, turning halfway through, until browned on 2 sides, about 5 minutes total.",
      "Meanwhile, remove parchment from baking sheet and discard. Transfer browned meatballs to bare sheet.",
      "In same skillet over medium heat, heat remaining 1 Tbsp. oil. Cook remaining 4 garlic cloves and 2 Tbsp. ginger, stirring, until fragrant, about 1 minute. Add curry paste and cook, stirring, until slightly darkened, 1 minute more.",
      "Stir in peanut butter and remaining coconut milk and 4 Tbsp. soy sauce until combined. Stir in bell peppers, then return meatballs to skillet and bring to a simmer. Cover and cook until meatballs are cooked through and peppers are tender, 3 to 5 minutes.",
      "Remove from heat and stir in lime juice. Taste and add more lime juice and salt, if needed. Top with peanuts, cilantro, and basil leaves."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "In our peanut chicken meatballs recipe, soft, tender meatballs are tossed in a creamy peanut sauce lightly spiked with Thai red curry paste, then topped with herbs and chopped peanuts for a colorful one-pan dinner that hits every note. "
  },
