      "1/4 cup brine from bread and butter pickles, plus pickles for serving",
      "1/4 cup Dijon mustard",
      "1/4 cup hot sauce, plus more for serving",
      "2 tbsp. apple cider vinegar",
      "1 cup (120 g.)&nbsp;all-purpose flour",
      "1/2 cup finely ground yellow cornmeal",
      "1 tbsp. cornstarch",
      "2 tsp. chili powder",
      "1 1/2 tsp. cayenne pepper",
      "1 tsp. onion powder",
      "1/2 tsp. baking powder",
      "1/2 tsp. garlic powder",
      "1/2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "Vegetable oil, for frying (2 to 3 cups)",
      "1 garlic clove",
      "1/2 cup vegan mayonnaise",
      "2 tsp. fresh lemon juice",
      "Freshly ground black pepper",
      "4 soft hamburger buns",
      "4 green lettuce leaves"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange tofu blocks in a single layer on a freezer-safe plate or in a large plastic container. Cover with plastic wrap or a lid. Freeze until solid, at least 5 hours and up to 1 month.",
      "Remove tofu from freezer and let defrost completely, about 4 hours on the counter or overnight in the refrigerator. Drain off any excess water.",
      "Line a baking sheet with several sheets of paper towels. Arrange tofu in a single layer on prepared sheet. Place a few more layers of paper towels and another baking sheet on top of tofu. Weight baking sheet with a few cookbooks or cans of beans. Let drain, changing paper towels when saturated with water, at least 1 hour and up to overnight in the refrigerator.",
      "In a shallow bowl, whisk pickle brine, mustard, hot sauce, and vinegar. In another shallow bowl, whisk flour, cornmeal, cornstarch, chili powder, pepper, onion powder, baking powder, garlic powder, and 1/2 tsp. salt.",
      "Cut each piece of tofu parallel to cutting board into 2 thinner planks; you should have 4 total. Working one at a time, coat tofu in flour mixture, then dip into brine mixture. Return to flour mixture, then pickle brine mixture, then dip one last time into flour mixture. Place on a clean plate.",
      "Into a large cast-iron skillet, pour oil to a depth of 1/2\". Heat over medium-high heat. When oil is hot and just starts to shimmer, reduce heat to medium.",
      "Fry tofu, turning once, until golden on both sides, about 5 minutes per side. Transfer to a paper towel–lined plate to drain.",
      "On a cutting board, smash garlic clove with the back of a knife; season with 1/2 tsp. salt. Continue to mash with the side of knife until garlic turns into a paste. Scrape paste into a small bowl and stir in mayonnaise and lemon juice; season with salt, if needed, and pepper.",
      "Spread garlic mayo on bottom halves of each bun. Top with lettuce, fried tofu, and pickles. Drizzle with hot sauce. Close with top bun."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "We replicated spicy fried chicken with protein-packed tofu and added cornmeal to the batter for extra crunch."
