  {
    "id": "1793153873990",
    "name": "Tofu Taco Bowls",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/mexican-tofu-taco-bowls-socialindex-web-1007-jg-del099925-68e80e80568ab.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.376xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "latin-american",
      "lunch",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "60 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "1 (14-oz.) pkg. extra-firm tofu",
      "6 cups plus 1 Tbsp. (or more)&nbsp;water, divided",
      "2 tbsp. plus 1 3/4 tsp. (or more) kosher salt, divided",
      "1 1/2 tsp. garlic powder",
      "1 1/2 tsp. paprika",
      "3/4 tsp. dried oregano",
      "3/4 tsp. ground cumin",
      "1/4 tsp. freshly ground black pepper",
      "3 tbsp. vegetable oil",
      "1 cup black beans, rinsed (from a 15.5-oz. can)",
      "1/2 cup thawed frozen corn",
      "1 tbsp. finely chopped fresh cilantro, plus whole leaves for serving",
      "1 tsp. fresh lime juice",
      "1 canned chipotle chile in adobo, finely chopped, plus 2 tsp. adobo sauce",
      "1/2 cup sour cream",
      "3 cups cooked quinoa",
      "1/2 cup store-bought or homemade pico de gallo",
      "1/2 avocado, thinly sliced",
      "Lime wedges, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "On a cutting board, holding a knife parallel to board, slice tofu block in half to yield 2 thinner blocks. Arrange in an 8\" baking dish in a single layer.",
      "In a kettle or medium pot, bring 6 cups water to a boil. Pour water over tofu; sprinkle 2 Tbsp. salt across water. Let sit for 20 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 425°. In a small bowl, stir garlic powder, paprika, oregano, cumin, black pepper, and 1 tsp. salt.",
      "Remove tofu from water, letting excess drip off, and transfer to a paper towel-lined plate. Blot dry with more paper towels (you may need a few rounds). Tear each slab into rough 1\" chunks (it’s okay if some pieces are a little smaller).",
      "Transfer tofu to a clean medium bowl and drizzle with oil. Add spice mix and gently toss to combine. Arrange tofu flat sides down on a large foil-lined baking sheet.",
      "Roast tofu until crisp, browned on the bottom, and slightly crisp on top, 23 to 28 minutes. Let cool slightly.",
      "Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, stir beans, corn, chopped cilantro, lime juice, and 1/2 tsp. salt.",
      "In a small bowl, stir chiptole chile, adobo sauce, sour cream, and 1/4 tsp. salt. Add 1 Tbsp. water and stir until combined. If a thinner sauce is desired, continue to add water, 1 tsp. at a time, until desired consistency is reached; season with salt, if needed. Refrigerate until ready to use.",
      "To build a bowl, spoon 3/4 cup quinoa into bottom of a bowl. Top with one-quarter of tofu, about 1/3 cup bean-corn mixture, 2 Tbsp. pico de gallo, and one-quarter of avocado. Drizzle with chipotle crema and top with whole cilantro leaves. Serve with lime wedges alongside."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "Loaded with quinoa, black beans, and taco-spiced tofu crumbles all drizzled with a chipotle crema, these bowls are quickly becoming my new taco Tuesday go-to."
  },
  {
    "id": "1793153874143",
    "name": "Miso Mushroom Crispy Rice",
    "image": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/del019924-crispy-miso-mushroom-rice-skillet-web-909-jg-index-67b62c8a735e5.jpg?crop=0.502xw:1.00xh;0.245xw,0&resize=1200:*",
    "categories": [
      "european",
      "asian",
      "dinner"
    ],
    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "45 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "5 cups plus 1 Tbsp. water, divided",
      "Kosher salt&nbsp;",
      "2 cups sushi rice&nbsp;",
      "6 tbsp. neutral oil, divided&nbsp;",
      "2 lb. shiitake mushrooms, thinly sliced, divided&nbsp;",
      "4 garlic cloves, finely chopped&nbsp;",
      "1 (1\") piece ginger, peeled, finely chopped&nbsp;",
      "5 tbsp. unsalted butter, divided",
      "4 scallions, green and white parts separated, thinly sliced, plus more for garnish&nbsp;",
      "1/2 cup dry white wine&nbsp;",
      "1/4 cup plus 2 Tbsp. low-sodium vegetable broth&nbsp;",
      "1/4 cup plus 3 Tbsp. red miso paste&nbsp;",
      "3 tbsp. chili crisp",
      "2 tbsp. unseasoned rice vinegar",
      "1 tbsp. hoisin sauce&nbsp;",
      "1/4 cup mayonnaise&nbsp;",
      "Toasted sesame seeds, for serving&nbsp;"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "In a small saucepan over high heat, bring 5 cups water and 1 Tbsp. salt to a boil.",
      "Meanwhile, rinse rice in a fine-mesh sieve until water runs clear. Add rice to boiling water, return to a boil, and gently stir to make sure no rice is stuck to bottom of pot. Cook, mostly undisturbed, until exterior is tender but middle of rice grain has a slight crunch, about 7 minutes. Drain in sieve, thoroughly rinse with cold water, and transfer to a large bowl.",
      "Into a large stainless steel or cast-iron skillet over medium heat, pour 3 Tbsp. oil and swirl to coat skillet. Add half of mushrooms and cook, stirring occasionally, until golden brown and crispy on the edges, 13 to 15 minutes. Add garlic and ginger and cook, stirring, until fragrant, 1 to 2 minutes more; season with a large pinch of salt. Transfer to a plate. Repeat with remaining 3 Tbsp. oil and mushrooms. Return all mushrooms to skillet and keep warm.",
      "In a medium skillet over medium heat, melt 2 Tbsp. butter. Add white scallion parts and cook, stirring frequently, until starting to soften, about 2 minutes. Add wine and cook, stirring occasionally, until liquid is reduced by about half, 1 to 2 minutes. Whisk in 1/4 cup broth and 1/4 cup miso until combined. Cook, stirring occasionally, until sauce is slightly thickened, 2 to 3 minutes. Transfer to bowl with rice and toss to combine.",
      "Wipe skillet clean and return to medium-low heat. Heat remaining 3 Tbsp. butter and 2 Tbsp. broth until butter melts. Gently spoon rice mixture into skillet on top of butter. (Do not pack the rice down.) Using a spoon handle, poke 6 to 8 holes about 1/2\" in diameter into rice to allow steam to escape. Wrap skillet lid in a clean kitchen towel and place towel-wrapped lid on top of rice. Cook 10 minutes, then rotate pan 180° and cook until rice is crackling and bottom is set and becomes deep brown, 8 to 10 minutes. Remove lid and invert rice onto a plate so crispy side is facing up.",
      "Meanwhile, in a small bowl, combine chili crisp, vinegar, hoisin, and remaining 3 Tbsp. miso. Pour half of miso mixture over mushrooms and toss to coat. Add mayonnaise to remaining miso mixture, then add remaining 1 Tbsp. water to make sauce easy to drizzle.",
      "Top rice with mushrooms and drizzle with miso mayo. Sprinkle with green scallion parts and sesame seeds."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "In this vegetarian dinner, sushi rice is cooked in until it creates a crispy base before being topped with miso mushrooms, and drizzled with spicy miso mayo.",
    "videos": [
      {
        "url": "https://mos-streaming.hearst.io/c73e4b8b-93c9-469c-b73a-c6ad4ee823e3/video_rover_16x9_1080p_hd_1740162839_23789.mp4",
        "title": "This Miso Mushroom Crispy Rice Is Even Better (!!) Than The OG That Inspired It",
        "thumbnailUrl": "https://hips.hearstapps.com/hmg-prod/images/del019924-crispy-miso-mushroom-rice-skillet-web-909-jg-index-67b62c8a735e5.jpg?crop=0.889xw:1.00xh;0.0561xw,0"
      }
    ]
