      "1 tbsp. unsweetened cocoa powder",
      "1/4 tsp. kosher salt",
      "2 cups heavy cream, divided"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Place chocolate in a large heatproof bowl. In a medium saucepan over low heat, cook butter and cocoa powder, stirring constantly, until butter is melted and smooth. Add salt and 1/2 cup cream. Increase heat to medium-high and bring to a simmer. Immediately pour cream mixture over chocolate and let sit, undisturbed, until mostly melted, about 5 minutes. (Make sure chocolate is submerged in cream, but do not stir; gently tilt bowl if necessary to redistribute it.)",
      "Meanwhile, in a medium bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed or a whisk, beat remaining 1 1/2 cups cream until soft peaks form. Refrigerate until ready to use.",
      "Using mixer or whisk, start drawing a small circle in center of chocolate mixture until just beginning to thicken and a dark, smooth vortex forms. Continue to beat in widening circles until mixture emulsifies into a uniformly thick and glossy ganache. Let sit at room temperature until no longer warm to the touch, about 5 minutes.",
      "Set aside about 1/2 cup whipped cream for serving; refrigerate until ready to use. Using a large spatula, fold one-third of chocolate ganache into remaining whipped cream until combined. Add remaining chocolate ganache and continue to fold until no streaks remain.",
      "Divide mousse among 6 ramekins or cups and refrigerate until set, about 40 minutes.",
      "Top with reserved whipped cream and more chips or shaved chocolate."
