      "dessert"
    ],
    "prepTime": "20 min",
    "cookTime": "100 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "Cooking spray",
      "6 oz. bittersweet chocolate, roughly chopped",
      "1/2 cup (1 stick) butter, cut into large chunks",
      "1 tsp. instant espresso powder",
      "1/4 cup hot water",
      "1 cup granulated sugar",
      "4 large eggs",
      "3/4 cup unsweetened cocoa powder (preferably Dutch-process)",
      "1/2 cup heavy cream",
      "1 cup semisweet chocolate chips",
      "Raspberries, for serving"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Place a rack in center of oven; preheat oven to 350°. Lightly coat an 8\" springform pan with cooking spray.",
      "Fill a small saucepan halfway with water and bring to a simmer over medium heat. Place bittersweet chocolate and butter in a heatproof bowl and set over saucepan, making sure bottom of bowl does not touch water. Cook, stirring, until chocolate and butter are melted and smooth. Remove bowl from heat.",
      "In a small bowl, dissolve espresso powder in hot water. Add espresso mixture and sugar to chocolate mixture and whisk until combined. Add eggs and whisk until incorporated, then stir in cocoa powder until smooth.",
      "Pour batter into prepared pan. Bake until cake is just set in center and a thin crust forms on top, about 35 minutes.",
      "Let cake cool in pan for 15 minutes. Remove sides of springform pan and let cake cool completely.",
      "In a small saucepan over medium heat, bring heavy cream to a simmer. Place chocolate chips in a heatproof bowl. Pour hot cream over chocolate chips and let stand 1 minute, then whisk until smooth.",
      "Pour ganache over cooled cake and spread evenly with an offset spatula. Refrigerate until ganache is set, if desired, about 10 minutes.",
      "Top with raspberries before serving."
    ],
    "servings": "10 serving(s)",
    "description": "The best part about this flourless chocolate cake is that it doesn't require any flour alternatives. It's just the perfect cake that happens to have zero flour. ",
