      "1 (14-oz.) package dried wide rice noodles",
      "1/2 cup canned full-fat coconut milk",
      "1/2 cup processed peanut butter",
      "1/4 cup reduced-sodium soy sauce",
      "1 large garlic clove, grated",
      "2 tbsp. sriracha, plus more to taste",
      "1 tbsp. brown sugar, plus more to taste",
      "2 tsp. finely grated lime zest",
      "2 tbsp. (or more) fresh lime juice",
      "3 tbsp. peanut or vegetable oil, divided",
      "1 1/2 tsp. kosher salt, plus more",
      "1/4 cup cornstarch",
      "8 oz. Chinese broccoli or broccolini, cut into 2”-long pieces",
      "Finely chopped raw peanuts and fresh cilantro or thinly sliced scallions, for serving (optional)"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Line a baking sheet with a few layers of paper towels, then arrange tofu on top in a single layer. Cover with more paper towels. Place second baking sheet on top. Add a heavy skillet, pot, or some cans to weigh it down. Let sit at room temperature at least 30 minutes and up to 1 hour.",
      "Meanwhile, in a large pot of boiling water, cook noodles according to package directions. Transfer to a colander (or large sieve), run under cold water for about 15 seconds, then drain.",
      "In a small bowl, whisk coconut milk, peanut butter, soy sauce, garlic, sriracha, brown sugar, and water. Whisk in lime zest and juice.",
      "In a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat, heat 2 Tbsp. oil. Transfer tofu to a medium bowl; season with 1 tsp. salt. Sprinkle cornstarch over, then toss cubes until coated.",
      "Arrange tofu in a single layer in skillet and cook, turning occasionally, until golden on most sides, 10 to 12 minutes total. Transfer to a large plate.",
      "Add broccoli; season with ½ tsp. salt. (Be careful, it will sputter.) Cover with a lid (or aluminum foil and cook, undisturbed, for 3 minutes. Uncover and continue to cook, stirring occasionally, until fork-tender, about 2 minutes more. Transfer to plate with tofu.",
      "In same skillet over medium heat, heat remaining 1 Tbsp. oil. Add noodles, spreading them out. Cover and cook, undisturbed, for 2 minutes. Pour in sauce and bring to a simmer; cook, stirring, until warmed through, about 1 minute.",
      "Stir in tofu and broccoli and remove from heat. Adjust seasonings with more salt, lime juice, brown sugar, and sriracha, if needed. If sauce is too thick, add water 1 Tbsp. at a time until loosened. Top with peanuts and cilantro (if using)."
    ],
    "servings": "4 serving(s)",
    "description": "In our Thai peanut crispy tofu, the extra-firm tofu cubes are coated in a rich, velvety sauce and tossed with chewy noodles and crisp-tender greens for a fun, easy vegetarian dinner."
  },
  {
    "id": "1793153891944",
