      "In a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat, heat 1 Tbsp. oil. Add onion and garlic; season with 1/2 tsp. salt. Cook, stirring occasionally, until softened and just starting to brown on the edges, 8 to 10 minutes.",
      "Add thyme and red pepper flakes and cook, stirring, until warmed through, about 2 minutes. Transfer onion mixture to a medium bowl; reserve skillet.",
      "Rinse salt off squash, then place in a clean kitchen towel. Continue to squeeze until most liquid is drained. Add squash to bowl with onion mixture. Add 1 Tbsp. oil and 1 tsp. salt and toss to combine.",
      "Transfer half of squash mixture to a 13\" x 9\" baking dish; spread to cover bottom of dish. Top with half of tomatoes; season with salt and pepper. Sprinkle with 1 Tbsp. sliced basil, then 1/2 cup Parmesan. Top with remaining squash and tomatoes; season with salt and pepper. Sprinkle with 1 Tbsp. sliced basil.",
      "Tightly cover dish with foil and bake until veggies are softened and juices are bubbling, 30 to 35 minutes.",
      "Uncover baking dish and continue to bake for 5 minutes more.",
      "Meanwhile, in a small bowl, mix lemon zest and remaining 1/2 cup Parmesan. Sprinkle Parmesan mixture over and continue to bake until topping is golden brown, 5 to 7 minutes.",
      "In reserved skillet over medium heat, heat remaining 1 Tbsp. oil. Toast panko, stirring frequently, until fragrant and deep golden brown, about 5 minutes.",
      "Sprinkle with panko. Immediately top casserole with burrata, tearing into pieces as you go; season with salt and pepper, if needed. Top with basil leaves."
