    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Peel beets and cut in half lengthwise. Slice crosswise into generous 1/4\"-thick half-moons.",
      "Transfer beets to a large microwave-safe bowl; season with salt and toss to coat. Add water and tightly cover with plastic wrap or a large plate.",
      "Microwave beets on High for 5 minutes. Remove from microwave, carefully uncover (steam will be hot!), and stir. Cover beets again and continue to microwave until beets are fork-tender, about 3 minutes more.&nbsp;Carefully uncover and let cool slightly.",
      "Meanwhile, in a small skillet over medium heat, toast coriander, allspice, and mustard seeds, stirring frequently, until fragrant, 1 to 2 minutes. Let cool. Transfer to a spice grinder or mill and pulse until coarsely ground.",
      "Transfer ground spices to a small bowl; add black pepper and toss to combine.",
      "On a work surface, arrange bread slices in a single layer. Spread butter on top of each slice of bread. Flip 4 slices buttered side down and spread plain side with 1 Tbsp. Russian dressing each. Sprinkle each with 1/2 tsp. ground spice mix.",
      "Flip remaining 4 slices buttered side down, then top each with 2 slices Swiss cheese and 5 to 6 beet slices. Sprinkle with 1/2 tsp. ground spice mix. Arrange sauerkraut on top. Close with remaining bread slices, dressing side down.",
      "Preheat a large nonstick skillet over medium heat. Add 2 sandwiches, arranging cheese side closest to skillet, and cook until golden brown, 2 to 3 minutes. Flip and continue to cook until golden brown on the other side and cheese is melty, 2 to 3 minutes more. Transfer sandwiches to a plate. Repeat with remaining sandwiches. Serve warm."
