      "Whisk in brown sugar (it will be grainy). Vigorously whisk in egg until mixture thickens but is still grainy, about 1 minute.",
      "In a medium bowl, whisk flour, cinnamon, baking soda, salt, and nutmeg. Using a rubber spatula, stir dry ingredients into butter mixture in saucepan just until no dry streaks remain.",
      "Transfer dough to a large bowl and tightly cover with plastic wrap. Refrigerate until well chilled, at least 4 hours and up to overnight.",
      "Arrange racks in upper and lower thirds of oven; preheat to 350°. Using a large<br>(3-Tbsp.) scoop or large spoon, scoop dough and arrange on 2 parchment-lined baking sheets, spacing 2\" apart.",
      "Bake cookies, rotating sheets top to bottom and front to back halfway through, until lightly golden, 10 to 12 minutes. Let cool slightly on sheets, then transfer to wire racks and let cool completely.",
      "In a small microwave-safe bowl, combine rum and 1 1/2 Tbsp. cold water. Sprinkle gelatin over and let sit until solidified, about 5 minutes.",
      "Meanwhile, in a medium (preferably metal) bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium speed, beat cream, confectioners’ sugar, and salt until thickened and just shy of stiff peaks, about 3 minutes.",
      "Microwave solidified gelatin until melted, for 10 seconds (no longer).",
      "With the mixer on low speed, slowly drizzle in gelatin mixture until incorporated. Increase mixer speed to medium-high and continue to beat until stiff, fluffy peaks form, 1 to 2 minutes more.",
      "Transfer frosting to a piping bag fitted with a small round tip or a resealable plastic bag with a corner snipped off. Pipe onto cookies in a swirl pattern. Dust with nutmeg."
    ],
    "servings": "12 serving(s)",
    "description": "Our hot brown buttered rum cookies borrow all the flavors of the classic cozy winter drink in a warm, nutty cookie."
