    "instructions": [
      "Using a paring knife, score an X into the bottom of each peach to help with peeling later. In a large saucepan, bring granulated sugar and 4 cups water to a boil, stirring until sugar is dissolved. Add peaches and reduce heat to medium-low. Simmer, stirring occasionally, until peaches are tender, 6 to 10 minutes. Let cool in syrup if not using right away. If using right away, using a slotted spoon, transfer peaches to a cutting board and let cool slightly.",
