    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "30 min",
    "ingredients": [
      "Cooking spray",
      "2 1/4 cups (270 g) all-purpose flour",
      "1 tsp. baking powder",
      "1/2 tsp. kosher salt",
      "1 1/4 cups (250 g) granulated sugar",
      "1 cup (2 sticks) unsalted butter, softened",
      "2 tsp. finely grated lemon zest",
      "1 large egg",
      "1 large egg yolk",
      "2 tbsp. limoncello",
      "1/2 cup (1 stick) unsalted butter, softened",
      "2 cups (226 g) confectioners’ sugar, divided",
      "2 tbsp. limoncello, plus more for serving",
      "8 oz. mascarpone, room temperature",
      "Finely grated lemon zest and white sprinkles, for topping"
    ],
    "instructions": [
      "Arrange a rack in center of oven; preheat to 350°. Line a 9\" x 9\" baking dish with parchment, leaving a 2\" overhang on 2 opposite sides. Grease parchment with cooking spray.",
      "In a medium bowl, whisk flour, baking powder, and salt.",
      "In a large bowl, using a handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat granulated sugar, butter, and lemon zest until fluffy and smooth, 1 to 2 minutes.",
      "Add egg and egg yolk, one at a time, beating to blend after each addition. Beat in limoncello. Add dry ingredients and mix with a wooden spoon until just combined. Spread batter in an even layer in prepared pan.",
      "Bake bar until golden and top feels set, 25 to 30 minutes. Let cool.",
      "In a large bowl, using handheld mixer on medium-high speed, beat butter and 1 cup confectioners’ sugar until smooth. Add limoncello and beat until combined. Add remaining 1 cup confectioners’ sugar and beat to combine. Fold in mascarpone.",
      "Spread frosting over cooled bar. Top with lemon zest and sprinkles. Cut into 16 squares, then cut each square into triangles. Make a small divot in the center of the triangles and pour a little limoncello into each."
    ],
    "servings": "16 serving(s)",
    "description": "Our limoncello cookie bars are sweet, sunny, and deeply lemony, thanks to the limoncello sugar cookie base and lemon mascarpone frosting."
